{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014SzAK7D2LWBUMYewvacKik","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Anchor R&D Surface v3 â€” \"Mission Control\" â€” Execution Log\n2\t\n3\t> Foreman appends per-wave EXECUTE / GATE / REVIEW / FIX / JUDGE entries here.\n4\t> Seeded by the Crucibleâ†’Foreman handoff on 2026-06-11. Frozen design:\n5\t> `MASTER-PLAN.md`. Plan: `IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md`. Gate: `python -m pytest -v`.\n6\t\n7\t## Handoff (2026-06-11)\n8\t\n9\t- Crucible Stage 0 (North Star locked), Stage 1 (Master Plan approved), Stage 2\n10\t  (10-wave plan, internal Shark-Tank converged given the Wave-1 ConPTY gate)\n11\t  complete.\n12\t- User-locked decisions: real ConPTY terminals (pywinpty; stdlib-only waiver for\n13\t  the terminal subsystem only); proactive cached summaries; git-worktree\n14\t  per-session isolation; one comprehensive build; **Wave-1 ConPTY-under-service\n15\t  spike HALTS to the user if it fails (no silent downgrade)**; status colors\n16\t  green=working / amber=needs-you-or-done / red=failed / grey=idle.\n17\t- Mid-Stage-2 addition: Wave 9 â€” brand the home page as a Ghost World Labs tool\n18\t  powered by NextGen Nuclear, using `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\GWL-M-Icon.svg` (ghost +\n19\t  â˜¢, palette matches the theme).\n20\t- Awaiting Foreman Wave 1 (the ConPTY-under-service spike â€” a hard gate).\n21\t\n22\t---\n23\t\n24\t## Wave 1 â€” ConPTY-under-service spike (HARD GATE) â€” GO (2026-06-11)\n25\t\n26\t**EXECUTE.** Created `pty_manager.py` (backend seam: real `pywinpty` backend +\n27\tdeterministic in-memory `stub` backend, env-selected by `ANCHOR_PTY_BACKEND`;\n28\t`winpty` imported LAZILY inside the pywinpty backend's `start` â€” `import\n29\tpty_manager` works with the native dep absent, surfacing `PtyUnavailable`).\n30\tManager core: `start/write/read_since/resize/kill`, cursor-stable like\n31\t`job_runner.tail`, `UnknownSession(KeyError)` on unknown ids, thread-safe live\n32\ttable. Added `tests/test_pty_manager.py` (stub-only, hermetic â€” no real process /\n33\tno pywinpty / no live claude) and `spike_conpty_service.py` (runnable empirical\n34\tspike).\n35\t\n36\t**GATE (orchestrator-run).** `python -m pytest -v` â†’ **409 passed, 1 skipped**\n37\t(baseline 399 + 10 new pty_manager tests). `import pty_manager` / `import\n38\tanchor_gui` both OK.\n39\t\n40\t**EMPIRICAL HARD-GATE PROOF (orchestrator-run, the user-gated requirement).**\n41\t1. `python spike_conpty_service.py` â†’ **SPIKE PASS, exit 0**: a real `pywinpty`\n42\t   ConPTY `cmd` child, launched under a faithfully simulated non-interactive\n43\t   `anchor` service context (full system env with `USERPROFILE`/`HOME` pinned to\n44\t   `C:\\Users\\john` and `APPDATA`/`LOCALAPPDATA` stripped), executed\n45\t   `set /a R=a*b` + `echo SPIKEOUT=!R!` and the COMPUTED product (never present in\n46\t   any typed input) round-tripped â€” proving command execution, not just input\n47\t   echo.\n48\t2. Corroboration with the real engine: launching **`claude`** itself through the\n49\t   pywinpty backend under the same simulated service env rendered the full\n50\t   interactive TUI (`âœ³ Claude Code v2.1.174`, `Opus 4.8 (1M context) â€¦ Claude\n51\t   Max`, input box, auto-mode) â€” ~1960 bytes of healthy TUI, finding the Claude\n52\t   **Max subscription** creds with no `APPDATA`. A real ConPTY claude session runs\n53\t   under the service context. **HALT condition NOT triggered.**\n54\t\n55\t**REVIEW (2 independent adversarial reviewers).** Both GO-WITH-NITS; neither could\n56\tbreak the lazy-import isolation, API contract, stub faithfulness, or\n57\tthread-safety. Agreed findings folded into FIX.\n58\t\n59\t**FIX (bounded, 1 iter).** (1) Declared `pywinpty` as an OPTIONAL extra\n60\t(`pyproject.toml` `[project.optional-dependencies] terminal`; core stays\n61\tstdlib-only). (2) `_PywinptyChild.kill` now tree-kills (`taskkill /T /F /PID`,\n62\tWindows-only, tolerated) to reap `claude`â†’`node` grandchildren, mirroring\n63\t`job_runner.cancel`; reader thread signaled to stop. (3) Bounded output buffer\n64\t(`MAX_BUFFER_CHARS`) in both backends, preserving absolute-cursor semantics\n65\t(`_total`/`_dropped`) so Wave-3 reattach/replay can't grow memory unbounded; new\n66\ttest added. (4) Hardened the spike's cmd proof to require command EXECUTION\n67\t(computed product distinct from input). Re-gate: **409 passed, 1 skipped**; spike\n68\tPASS exit 0.\n69\t\n70\t**Known seams recorded for later waves (not Wave-1 reworks):** `read_since` uses\n71\tcharacter offsets returning `str` (pywinpty `read()` returns decoded str) â€”\n72\tWave 3/4 must handle byte-framing when wiring xterm.js; a manager-`kill`ed session\n73\tdrops from the live table so its final buffer isn't drainable as `status:\"dead\"`\n74\t(only self-exited children report `dead`) â€” Wave 3/4's kill-confirm + status-color\n75\tUI may want a final-drain contract.\n76\t\n77\t**Verdict: GO.** Committed on branch `foreman/rnd-surface-v3`.\n78\t\n79\t---\n80\t\n81\t## Wave 2 â€” Durable session registry + git-worktree isolation â€” GO (2026-06-11)\n82\t\n83\t**EXECUTE.** `session_registry.py` â€” durable, persisted-under-`.anchor/`\n84\t(`sessions.json`, atomic tmp+`os.replace` under `paths.WRITE_LOCK`) registry of\n85\tmanaged sessions `{session_id, project_id, lane, backend, worktree_path, branch,\n86\tstatus, created_at, label}`; best-effort load (corrupt/torn/missing â†’ empty);\n87\t`register/get/list(filter)/update/remove`; status constants mapped to the locked\n88\tcolors (runningâ†’green, needs-attention/doneâ†’amber, failedâ†’red, idleâ†’grey);\n89\tinjectable `reconcile(live_session_ids, ...)` re-statuses dead sessions + surfaces\n90\torphan worktrees. `worktrees.py` â€” `create_worktree`/`remove_worktree`/\n91\t`reap_orphans` via stdlib `subprocess`, worktrees under a git-ignored managed base\n92\t(`paths.data_dir()/.anchor/worktrees/<sid>`, overridable via\n93\t`ANCHOR_WORKTREE_BASE`), path-containment guard, never raises. Hermetic tests use\n94\ttemp git repos + temp base.\n95\t\n96\t**GATE (orchestrator-run).** `python -m pytest -v` â†’ **429 passed, 1 skipped**.\n97\tBuild repo verified untouched: `git worktree list` shows only the main tree;\n98\t`git branch --list 'anchor/session/*'` empty.\n99\t\n100\t**REVIEW (2 independent adversarial reviewers).** Both GO-WITH-NITS. Reviewer A\n101\tverified durability/atomicity, corrupt-store survival, genuine disk restart\n102\tround-trip, reconcile correctness, isolation-test integrity (no cheats). Reviewer\n103\tB (safety focus) proved no path-traversal/absolute-id escape from the managed\n104\tbase, no `shell=True`, build repo never touched, `reap_orphans(empty)` can't prune\n105\tthe main tree â€” but found a MAJOR branch-naming bug + branch litter.\n106\t\n107\t**FIX (bounded, 1 iter).** (1) MAJOR: `branch_for` no longer truncates to 12\n108\tchars (collision) â€” now full-id slug + 16-hex SHA-1; `create_worktree` ALWAYS\n109\tcreates a fresh branch (`git worktree add -b <branch> <path> <HEAD>`) and returns\n110\t`branch-exists` rather than silently attaching to an existing branch's tip; new\n111\tshared-12-char-prefix test proves distinct branches + isolation. (2) MINOR:\n112\t`remove_worktree` now `git branch -D`s the per-session branch (tolerated) so the\n113\treal repo doesn't accumulate `anchor/session/*` litter. (3) Test-integrity: the\n114\tmislabeled `test_remove_refuses_unsafe_path` now actually drives a traversal +\n115\tabsolute id and asserts `reason=='unsafe-path'` with an outside sentinel\n116\tsurviving. (4) Clarified the `reconcile` `applied` docstring. Re-gate: **429\n117\tpassed, 1 skipped**; zero repo leakage.\n118\t\n119\t**Seam for Wave 3.** `start_session` flow: mint sid â†’ `worktrees.create_worktree`\n120\tâ†’ `pty_manager.start(cwd=path)` â†’ `session_registry.register_session(...,\n121\tstatus=RUNNING)`. On kill: `update_session` then `remove_worktree`. On startup:\n122\t`reconcile(live=pty_manager.live_sessions())` + `reap_orphans` + `ensure_gitignored`.\n123\tWave 3 must reconcile the pty_manager opaque id with the registry session_id\n124\t(reuse the PTY id as session_id is simplest).\n125\t\n126\t**Verdict: GO.**\n127\t\n128\t---\n129\t\n130\t## Wave 3 â€” ConPTY terminal manager + transport + auth â€” GO (2026-06-11)\n131\t\n132\t**EXECUTE.** `terminal_session.py` ties Wave-1 PTY + Wave-2 registry/worktrees into\n133\ta live service: `start_session(project_id, lane, backend)` (creates worktree â†’\n134\tlaunches a BARE interactive PTY in it via `pty_manager.start([backend],\n135\tcwd=worktree)` â†’ registers ONE id = the reused PTY id, `status=running`),\n136\t`attach` (reattach replays the full retained screen buffer via `read_since(.,0)`),\n137\t`input`/`resize`/`read_since`, `kill` (reap PTY + remove worktree + terminal\n138\tstatus), `list_sessions`. Transport in `anchor_gui.py`: a stdlib hand-rolled\n139\t**WebSocket** `GET /api/rnd/term_ws` (pure RFC-6455 codec `ws_accept_key`/\n140\t`encode_text_frame`/`decode_frames`; 101 upgrade then bidirectional pump) + the\n141\t**SSE-out** `GET /api/rnd/term_stream2` and **POST-in** `term_input2` fallback,\n142\tplus lifecycle POSTs `term_start`/`term_kill`/`term_resize`. New names avoid\n143\tcolliding with the v2 stream-json REPL endpoints.\n144\t\n145\t**GATE (orchestrator-run).** `python -m pytest -v` â†’ **449 passed, 1 skipped**.\n146\t`ws_accept_key('dGhlIHNhbXBsZSBub25jZQ==')` == the RFC-6455 reference\n147\t`s3pPLMBiTxaQ9kYGzzhZRbK+xOo=`. Build repo untouched (`git worktree list` = main\n148\tonly; no `anchor/session/*` branches).\n149\t\n150\t**REVIEW (2 independent adversarial reviewers).** Both GO-WITH-NITS; no BLOCKER.\n151\tReviewer A (security/transport) verified â€” by code, tests, AND live 401 probes â€”\n152\tthat auth is enforced BEFORE any side effect on ALL six terminal endpoints (WS\n153\trejected 401 before the 101 upgrade; GET transports gate via `_term_token_ok`\n154\tquery-param token; POSTs ride the do_POST middleware), the codec is alloc-safe,\n155\tthe pumps are bounded (no hang). Reviewer B (service) verified rollback-safe\n156\tlifecycle, one-id-per-session under concurrency, kill isolation (can't remove the\n157\twrong worktree), pure detach, and full Wave-3 G/W/T coverage.\n158\t\n159\t**FIX (bounded, 1 iter).** (1) MAJOR: `start_session` now rolls back the PTY +\n160\tworktree if `register_session` raises (no reconcile-invisible orphan). (2) Clamped\n161\t`poll`âˆˆ[0.01,1.0]/`max_ticks`âˆˆ[1,5000] on both new GET transports\n162\t(authed-self-DoS). (3) `MAX_WS_FRAME`=1 MiB cap in `decode_frames` (close on\n163\toversized; no unbounded inbuf). (4) `attach` now surfaces `dropped`/`truncated` so\n164\ta reattach is honest about discarded scrollback. (5) Unknown-lane rejected before\n165\tany worktree/PTY. (6) WS fragmentation reassembly (FIN handling) +\n166\tunmasked-client-frame â†’ protocol-error close (RFC Â§5.4/Â§5.1), gated behind\n167\t`require_mask` to keep server-frame decode tests valid. Re-gate: **449 passed, 1\n168\tskipped**; WS reference key still correct; zero repo leakage.\n169\t\n170\t**Seam for Wave 4 (UI).** Endpoints: `POST term_start\n171\t{project_id,lane,backend,label?}â†’{ok,session}`, `GET term_ws?session=&token=`\n172\t(live), `GET term_stream2?session=&token=` (fallback), `POST term_input2\n173\t{session,data}`, `POST term_resize {session,cols,rows}`, `POST term_kill\n174\t{session}`. Statusâ†’color: running=green Â· needs-attention/done=amber Â· failed=red\n175\tÂ· idle=grey. Repopulate via `terminal_session.list_sessions(project_id=...)`;\n176\tfirst paint via `attach()` (`buffer`/`cursor`/`status`/`dropped`). Known seam:\n177\t`read_since` returns decoded `str` sent as UTF-8 WS text frames â€” fine for\n178\txterm.js text; binary control-seq framing is a possible Wave-4 refinement.\n179\t\n180\t**Verdict: GO.**\n181\t\n182\t---\n183\t\n184\t## Wave 4 â€” Stacking window-manager UI â€” GO (2026-06-11)\n185\t\n186\t**EXECUTE.** Front-end in `anchor_gui.py` (`render_project_window_html` CSS/HTML +\n187\t`_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS` RAW string): a status-colored **session button bar**\n188\t(`#sessionBar`, one `.sessbtn` per live registry session, `.sess-dot--green/\n189\t--amber/--red/--grey` driven by `_statusColor()` â€” exactly running=green,\n190\tneeds-attention/done=amber, failed=red, idle=grey), a **stacking window manager**\n191\t(`#windowLayer`/`.termwin`: brick-offset stacking, draggable titlebar, resize\n192\thandle, minimize that only collapses â€” never kills, X = `killSession` with an\n193\t\"Are you sure?\" `confirm(...)` gating `POST term_kill`). Each window mounts xterm.js\n194\tover `term_ws?session=&token=` (SSE `term_stream2` fallback), inputâ†’`term_input2`,\n195\tresizeâ†’`term_resize`, all token-aware (`?token=` from localStorage; token never\n196\tbaked into served HTML). New read-only `GET /api/rnd/term_sessions?project_id=`\n197\treturns a safe projection (NO `worktree_path`/`branch`/`project_id`) for the\n198\trepopulate-on-load hook (`loadSessions` on DOMContentLoaded). The v2 console\n199\tdrawer is left intact.\n200\t\n201\t**GATE (orchestrator-run).** `python -m pytest -v` â†’ **455 passed, 1 skipped**.\n202\tIndependently verified: `render_project_window_html(<real pid>)` (48 KB) and\n203\t`generate_html` (202 KB) both have **0 leaked `{{`/`}}`**; all Wave-4 ids/classes/\n204\tendpoint refs present; `git worktree list` = main only.\n205\t\n206\t**REVIEW (2 independent adversarial reviewers).** Reviewer A (UI/plan-fidelity):\n207\t**GO**, no findings â€” status mapping un-inverted, kill-confirm un-bypassable,\n208\tminimize keeps the session running, transport/token wiring safe, repopulate works,\n209\tno scope creep, v2 drawer intact. Reviewer B (endpoint security/XSS/braces):\n210\t**GO-WITH-NITS** â€” verified 0 brace leaks on served output, `term_sessions` strips\n211\t`worktree_path` (live-probed), no reachable unescaped `innerHTML` sink (bar/titlebar\n212\tuse `textContent`/`_esc`), token never in HTML, all mutators POST-authed.\n213\t\n214\t**FIX (bounded, 1 iter).** (1) Added an XSS-regression test: a stub session with\n215\tlabel `<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>` is served inert (application/json) and never\n216\tembedded as a raw HTML sink in the server-rendered window (guards a future\n217\t`innerHTML` regression). (2) Added `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` to all JSON\n218\tresponses (`_send_json`). Re-gate: **455 passed, 1 skipped**.\n219\t\n220\t**Seam for Wave 5/6.** `MANAGED` map + `_statusColor()` reusable for the Wave-5\n221\tthin-row status dots; `newTermSession(lane, backend)` is the launch path Wave 6\n222\tenriches with launch-from-summary seeding; the window-manager surface is\n223\tindependent of the v2 console drawer so Wave-6 inline summaries coexist.\n224\t\n225\t**Verdict: GO.**\n226\t\n227\t---\n228\t\n229\t## Wave 5 â€” Thin project rows + accurate proactive project summary â€” GO (2026-06-11)\n230\t\n231\t**EXECUTE.** `summarizer.py` gains a PROJECT-summary path mirroring (reusing, not\n232\tforking) the session pipeline: `summarize_project(folder, pid, force=False)` /\n233\t`load_cached_project` seed from CLAUDE.md/README/Anchor.md + newest\n234\t`planning/**/{MASTER,IMPLEMENTATION}-PLAN.md` + pinned deliverables â†’ generate-twice\n235\tthrough the `ANCHOR_RUNNER_CMD`/job_runner seam (never live claude) â†’ the existing\n236\tgrounding filter â†’ cache `.anchor/projects/<id>/project-summary.json(.md)`\n237\t(generate-once; `force=True` regenerates; a failed run never poisons the cache).\n238\tThe dashboard RENDER path only READS the cache (`load_cached_project`), falling\n239\tback to the blurb â€” it never runs the model. Proactive generation triggers on\n240\t`POST /api/rnd/rescan` (â†’ `discover_and_adopt` â†’ `_trigger_project_summary`, a\n241\tbackground daemon thread gated by `_PROACTIVE_SUMMARY_ENABLED`/`ANCHOR_PROACTIVE_SUMMARY`).\n242\t`anchor_gui.render_project_tile_html` rewritten to a **thin full-width `.rnd-row`**\n243\t(status dot Â· name Â· cached-summary-or-blurb Â· per-lane mini-counts Â· `.rnd-kebab`\n244\tlifecycle menu); row click â†’ `openProjectWindow`.\n245\t\n246\t**GATE (orchestrator-run).** `python -m pytest -v` â†’ **467 passed, 1 skipped**.\n247\t0 leaked `{{`/`}}` in the projects view + generate_html.\n248\t\n249\t**REVIEW (2 independent adversarial reviewers).** Both GO-WITH-NITS. Reviewer A\n250\tverified â€” with a live concurrency proof â€” generate-once/cache/force, no\n251\tcache-poison on failure, grounding drops ungrounded claims, the render path never\n252\truns the model, and (the hard-scrutinized axis) the **proactive-on-rescan path is\n253\tgenuinely tested end-to-end** (a test enables the flag, POSTs rescan, and polls for\n254\tthe cached summary). Reviewer B verified the thin-row markup, summary precedence,\n255\tHTML-escaping (XSS-safe incl. attribute-breakout), brace hygiene, status-dot\n256\tsemantics, and confirmed the `test_set_blurb` tileâ†’row change was a legitimate\n257\tplan-required migration (load-bearing assertion kept), not weakening.\n258\t\n259\t**FIX (bounded, 1 iter).** (1) MINOR: removed genuinely-dead `.rnd-tile`/\n260\t`.rnd-tile-head`/`.rnd-effort` CSS (grep-confirmed emitted by ZERO render paths)\n261\tand retargeted the stale `test_tile_has_lifecycle_controls_and_multiwindow_open`\n262\tto assert the real `.rnd-row`/kebab/`openProjectWindow` structure â€” so the guard is\n263\tmeaningful again (also resolved the cross-file `rnd-tile` contradiction). (2)\n264\tSynced `.anchor/.gitignore` with an explicit allow-list line for\n265\t`project-summary.json/.md`. (3) Added a project-summary concurrency regression test\n266\t(generate-once under 2 racing threads). Re-gate: **467 passed, 1 skipped**.\n267\t\n268\t**Accepted residual risk (recorded).** The grounding filter is deterministic\n269\tterm-overlap, not semantic (Reviewer A: a hallucinated claim CAN survive against a\n270\tlarge project corpus). This is the same v2-inherited filter; mitigations\n271\t(generate-twice fusion + min-2-grounded-terms + 0.7 ratio) remain. Re-architecting\n272\tgrounding to be semantic is out of this build's scope.\n273\t\n274\t**Verdict: GO.**\n275\t\n276\t---\n277\t\n278\t## Wave 6 â€” In-place expandable session summaries â€” GO (2026-06-11)\n279\t\n280\t**EXECUTE.** `summarizer.py` enriches the structured SESSION summary to the locked\n281\tÂ§B shape: `when_run` (real session timestamp), `what_was_asked` (bounded\n282\tseed/prompt), `north_star` (lifted from the session's MASTER-PLAN member),\n283\t`effort` (`_aggregate_effort` sums the session's member job cost records â†’\n284\t`{tokens, wall_clock_ms, cost_usd, runs}`; **imported/discovered â†’ `null` =\n285\t\"imported â€” no run metrics\", never fabricated**) â€” all cached in `summary.json` +\n286\t`render_markdown`. `anchor_gui.py`: clicking a session expands an **inline\n287\taccordion** (no `/summary` navigation â€” `openSummary` is now dead/back-compat) that\n288\tfetches the new read-only `GET /api/rnd/session_summary?pid&lane&session` (cache â†’\n289\t`ready`; uncached â†’ background gen + `generating`, never a synchronous model run)\n290\tand renders when/what/North-Star/effort + **doc links that open rendered markdown\n291\tin a new tab** (the only new-tab, via `/report`Â·`/artifact`). A **\"Launch new\n292\tsession\"** button in the panel calls the Wave-4 path (`newTermSession` â†’\n293\t`term_start`) carrying `seed_session` (the Wave-7 seam). Proactive session-summary\n294\tgeneration triggers on rescan (background, gated).\n295\t\n296\t**GATE (orchestrator-run).** `python -m pytest -v` â†’ **478 passed, 1 skipped**.\n297\t0 leaked `{{`/`}}` in the project window + dashboard.\n298\t\n299\t**REVIEW (2 independent adversarial reviewers).** Both GO-WITH-NITS; no\n300\tBLOCKER/MAJOR. Reviewer A proved the **honesty contract** (no imported/discovered\n301\tsession can surface fabricated effort â€” the would-be-MAJOR axis), correct effort\n302\taggregation, grounded content fields, and a read-only non-blocking endpoint.\n303\tReviewer B confirmed the accordion genuinely replaces `/summary` navigation\n304\t(`openSummary` dead, enforced by a negative test), doc links are the only new tab,\n305\tlaunch-from-panel is token-aware, escaping is XSS-safe (incl. the href sink), and\n306\tthe tests are additive (no `/summary` test weakened).\n307\t\n308\t**FIX (bounded, 1 iter).** (1) Strengthened the effort test to drive a REAL\n309\t`fake_claude --result` envelope end-to-end (envelope â†’ `_cost_from_envelope` â†’\n310\t`attach_cost` â†’ `_aggregate_effort`), asserting the non-null aggregated\n311\t`{tokens=142, wall_clock_ms=4567, runs}`. (2) Added symmetric `_unsafe_path_seg(pid)`\n312\trejection on the endpoint. (3) Unknown pid/session now returns a terminal\n313\t`status:\"unknown\"` (panel stops polling + shows \"summary unavailable\") instead of\n314\tspinning on \"generating\" forever. Re-gate: **478 passed, 1 skipped**.\n315\t\n316\t**Seam for Wave 7.** The launch-from-panel button puts `seed_session` (source\n317\tsession id) into the `term_start` payload; `start_session` accepts-but-does-not-yet-\n318\tconsume it. Wave 7 wires it through to most-recent-plan-set discovery + worktree\n319\tpre-staging + the `Anchor.md` handoff record.\n320\t\n321\t**Verdict: GO.**\n322\t\n323\t---\n324\t\n325\t## Wave 7 â€” Stage handoffs â€” GO (2026-06-12)\n326\t\n327\t**EXECUTE.** New `handoff.py`: `discover_recent_plan_set(folder, pid,\n328\tsource_session_id=)` (newest planning session with a MASTER+IMPL plan pair;\n329\t`seed_session` overrides to a specific session; falls back to the newest\n330\t`discovery.json` `by_lane.planning` group), `propose_handoff` (build lane â†’\n331\t`{has_plan_set, plan_set, message}`), `prime_worktree` (writes a passive\n332\t`HANDOFF.md` INSIDE the worktree referencing the plan doc paths â€” which already\n333\texist in the checkout â€” never copies contents, never auto-seeds a skill), and\n334\t`record_handoff` (atomic, structure-only handoff record in `discovery.json`).\n335\t`anchor_gui.py`: read-only `GET /api/rnd/handoff_proposal`; `term_start` on a build\n336\tlaunch discoversâ†’primesâ†’records after `start_session`, gracefully skipping when no\n337\tplan set exists. Consumes the Wave-6 `seed_session` seam.\n338\t\n339\t**GATE (orchestrator-run).** `python -m pytest -v` â†’ **493 passed, 1 skipped**;\n340\t`git worktree list` = main only.\n341\t\n342\t**REVIEW (2 independent adversarial reviewers).** Reviewer A returned **NO-GO** with\n343\tan empirically-proven **BLOCKER**: the handoff record was non-durable â€”\n344\t`anchor_marker.write_anchor_md` rewrote `discovery.json` from `scan.to_dict()`\n345\t(which omits `handoffs`), so any rescan / `GET /project/<id>` open DESTROYED the\n346\trecord (recordâ†’rescanâ†’`handoffs` gone), defeating the Done-when; the GREEN gate\n347\tmasked it because no test recordedâ†’rescannedâ†’re-asserted (MAJOR coverage gap).\n348\tReviewer B (GO-WITH-NITS) verified correct discovery/seed-override, graceful\n349\tdegradation, traversal-safe endpoint (no abs-path/contents leak), bare-PTY contract\n350\tintact â€” and flagged the proposal endpoint as a dead UI (offerâ†’confirm half-wired)\n351\t+ untested HTTP wiring + unsanitized lane/seed.\n352\t\n353\t**FIX (bounded, 1 iter).** (1) BLOCKER: `write_anchor_md` now READS the existing\n354\tsidecar and MERGES `scan.to_dict()` with preserved non-scan keys (`handoffs`),\n355\twriting atomically; `_sidecar_changed` compares only scan-owned keys (minus\n356\t`generated_at`) so a no-op rescan neither churns nor drops `handoffs`. Regression\n357\ttest `test_handoff_survives_rescan` (record â†’ rescan â†’ no-op rescan, `handoffs`\n358\tsurvives) â€” the exact zero-coverage scenario. **Independently re-verified by the\n359\torchestrator** (record:True, rescan#1:True, no-op#2:True). (2) Added end-to-end HTTP\n360\ttests: real `POST term_start` build launch â†’ `HANDOFF.md` in worktree +\n361\t`discovery.json` record (survives), and a `handoff_proposal` endpoint test. (3)\n362\tWired the offerâ†’confirm loop: a build launch fetches `handoff_proposal` and\n363\t`confirm(\"Execute on this plan set?â€¦\")` before priming (endpoint no longer dead).\n364\t(4) Symmetric `_unsafe_path_seg` on lane/seed_session. Re-gate: **493 passed, 1\n365\tskipped**.\n366\t\n367\t**Seam for Wave 8/10.** Handoff records live in `discovery.json` (now rescan-durable)\n368\tâ€” Wave 10's healthcheck/distro-scan can rely on them. The general \"Launch new\n369\tsession\" seeds prior-stage outputs via `seed_session`.\n370\t\n371\t**Verdict: GO** (after the BLOCKER fix).\n372\t\n373\t---\n374\t\n375\t## Wave 8 â€” Runnable Anchor deliverable (ephemeral preview) â€” GO (2026-06-12)\n376\t\n377\t**EXECUTE.** `anchor_gui.py` is pinned as the Anchor deliverable\n378\t(`ensure_anchor_deliverable` â†’ `deliverables.pin_deliverable`, idempotent, now\n379\tpin-if-absent). New `preview_server.py`: `start_preview` picks an OS-assigned free\n380\tport (hard-guarded `!= 8777`, belt-and-suspenders), launches `python anchor_gui.py\n381\t--port <port> --no-browser` with an ISOLATED env (temp `ANCHOR_DATA_DIR`, loopback\n382\tbind, token stripped) from the live checkout, health-checks `http://127.0.0.1:<port>/`\n383\t(bounded), returns the URL; `stop_preview` tree-kills (`taskkill /T /F`) + scrubs the\n384\ttemp dir; `list_previews`/`reap_orphans` reconcile dead previews on restart;\n385\tpersisted to `.anchor/previews.json`. Auth-gated `POST /api/rnd/preview_start`/\n386\t`preview_stop`; read-only `GET /api/rnd/previews` (safe projection, no abs paths).\n387\tDeliverables-lane UI gets Run (opens the preview URL in a new tab) + Stop.\n388\t\n389\t**GATE (orchestrator-run).** First full-suite run was **RED** â€” the sub-agent's\n390\tsubset missed it: the new test embedded a `token=\"tok-prev\"` literal that the\n391\tdistro no-secrets scan flags as `auth-token-value` (5 `test_distro_scan` failures).\n392\tOrchestrator fixed it (swap to the allowlisted placeholder `tok-123`, as the Wave-3\n393\ttests do). Re-gate: **502 passed, 1 skipped**. Live `:8777` service verified\n394\t**Running and untouched** (PID unchanged); **0 orphan preview processes** after the\n395\trun.\n396\t\n397\t**REVIEW (2 independent adversarial reviewers).** Reviewer A (safety): **GO** â€”\n398\tno path can bind/disturb 8777 (OS-ephemeral bind + double `!=8777` re-assert +\n399\thardcoded `--port` argv), data isolated to a temp dir, real tree-kill reap,\n400\tauth-before-spawn, bounded health-check, graceful TOCTOU handling. Reviewer B\n401\t(wiring): **GO-WITH-NITS** â€” idempotent pinning, deliverable shown, Run/Stop\n402\ttoken-aware + XSS-safe, 0 brace leaks, persisted structure-only registry.\n403\t\n404\t**FIX (bounded, 1 iter).** (1) `ensure_anchor_deliverable` now pins ONLY IF ABSENT\n405\t(no per-render write churn under `WRITE_LOCK`). (2) `GET /api/rnd/previews` projects\n406\tto a safe subset omitting absolute `data_dir`/`folder_path` (consistent with\n407\t`term_sessions`), with a test. (3) Documented the live-checkout-by-design decision\n408\t(data+port isolation is the safety contract; the deliverable IS the in-repo\n409\t`anchor_gui.py`). Re-gate: **502 passed, 1 skipped**; live service still untouched,\n410\t0 orphans.\n411\t\n412\t**Seam for Wave 10.** `preview_server.py` is pure stdlib (no distro-scan exception\n413\tneeded). Healthcheck v3 walk can use `pick_free_port` (never-8777) + `reap_orphans`\n414\twith an injected dead-pid record to avoid spawning at the 5 AM check. CLI mirror\n415\tcandidates: `rnd preview-start/-stop/-list`.\n416\t\n417\t**Verdict: GO.**\n418\t\n419\t---\n420\t\n421\t## Wave 9 â€” Ghost World Labs branding on the Home page â€” GO (2026-06-12)\n422\t\n423\t**EXECUTE.** Vendored `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\GWL-M-Icon.svg` â†’ `vendor/brand/gwl-m-icon.svg`\n424\t(real on-disk copy,