{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_017432uRr2WQFmDGmpamPHuD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Summary of the **rnd-v3** build trio session, grounded in the Execution Log:\n\n## Anchor R&D Surface v3 â€” \"Mission Control\" (build trio session)\n\n**Outcome**\n- All ten waves landed GREEN; the final gate was **529 passed, 1 skipped** (the lone skip is an unrelated host-conditional symlink test, not a v3 skip).\n- Built on branch `foreman/rnd-surface-v3`. **NOT merged to master and the live `anchor` service NOT restarted** â€” deploy (merge + elevated `nssm restart anchor`) was left as the user's call.\n- Crucible handed off on 2026-06-11 (Stage 0 North Star locked, Stage 1 Master Plan approved, Stage 2 10-wave plan converged); waves executed 2026-06-11 â†’ 2026-06-12.\n\n**Per-wave claims**\n- **Wave 1 (HARD GATE) â€” ConPTY substrate.** `pty_manager.py` with a backend seam (real `pywinpty` + deterministic in-memory `stub`, env-selected by `ANCHOR_PTY_BACKEND`); `winpty` lazy-imported and isolated to that one module. The empirical spike proved a real `pywinpty` `claude` TUI runs under a simulated non-interactive `anchor`-service context (computed product round-tripped, proving execution not just echo) â€” the HALT condition was never triggered. Gate: 409 passed, 1 skipped.\n- **Wave 2 â€” durable session registry + git-worktree isolation.** `session_registry.py` (atomic `.anchor/sessions.json`, statusâ†’color map) + `worktrees.py` (per-session worktrees under a git-ignored managed base). A reviewer caught a MAJOR branch-naming collision bug (12-char truncation) â€” fixed to full-id slug + 16-hex SHA-1 with always-fresh branches. Gate: 429 passed.\n- **Wave 3 â€” terminal service + transport + auth.** `terminal_session.py` ties PTY + registry + worktrees; transport is a stdlib hand-rolled WebSocket (`term_ws`, verified against the RFC-6455 reference key) plus SSE-out/POST-in fallback. Auth enforced before any side effect on all six endpoints. Gate: 449 passed.\n- **Wave 4 â€” stacking window-manager UI.** Status-colored session button bar + draggable/resizable/minimizable terminal windows mounting xterm.js; X=kill-with-confirm, minimize keeps the session running. Added an XSS-regression test + `nosniff` header. Gate: 455 passed.\n- **Wave 5 â€” thin project rows + proactive project summary.** `summarizer.summarize_project` (generate-twice through the runner seam, grounding-filtered, cached); render path reads cache only, generation is background-on-rescan. Gate: 467 passed. Recorded residual risk: the grounding filter is deterministic term-overlap, not semantic.\n- **Wave 6 â€” in-place expandable session summaries.** Inline accordion (when/what/North-Star/effort + doc links), replacing `/summary` navigation; imported/discovered sessions show `null` effort (\"no run metrics\", never fabricated). Gate: 478 passed.\n- **Wave 7 â€” stage handoffs.** New `handoff.py` (discover most-recent plan set â†’ `prime_worktree` writes a passive `HANDOFF.md` â†’ durable `discovery.json` record). A reviewer returned **NO-GO** with a proven BLOCKER: the handoff record was destroyed on rescan because `write_anchor_md` omitted `handoffs`; fixed by read-merge-write + a `test_handoff_survives_rescan` regression test. Gate: 493 passed.\n- **Wave 8 â€” runnable Anchor deliverable.** `preview_server.py` launches an ephemeral `anchor_gui.py` preview on an OS-assigned port hard-guarded `!= 8777`, isolated temp data dir, tree-killed/reaped. A distro no-secrets-scan caught a `tok-prev` literal (the sub-agent subset missed it); fixed to the allowlisted placeholder. Live `:8777` verified untouched, 0 orphans. Gate: 502 passed.\n- **Wave 9 â€” Ghost World Labs branding.** Vendored `gwl-m-icon.svg`, traversal-safe `/vendor/brand/` route (probed across 11 raw-socket traversal vectors â€” all 404), GWL favicon + sidebar lockup + \"Powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\". Both reviewers GO, no findings. Gate: 515 passed.\n- **Wave 10 â€” CLI mirror + healthcheck + distro scan (closing wave).** `anchor.py` read-only `rnd term-sessions`/`previews`/`handoff`; `check_rnd_v3_surface` walks the surface fully stubbed; `distro.py` AST import-scan declaring the single file-scoped `pywinpty` exception. Gate: 529 passed.\n\n**Process claims**\n- Every wave passed an **orchestrator-run** ground-truth gate (never a sub-agent's pasted output) plus **two independent adversarial reviewers**.\n- The adversarial loop caught and fixed real pre-merge defects â€” notably the Wave-7 handoff-durability BLOCKER and the Wave-8 distro secret-literal regression the sub-agent's test subset missed."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":638,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15514,"cache_read_input_tokens":96438,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15514},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6758890-ae02-4015-a628-f761c2091460","uuid":"98527ce9-ca3b-4625-af37-f7ec041bc1cc","request_id":"req_011CcJoGxX13ydVmdtDeEMHz"}
